.policy "ruff-n818-error-suffix-on-exception-name" revision 2
.description "Name custom exception classes with an Error suffix, as PEP 8 recommends, unless the exception does not signal an error."
.language python
.mode steer
.scope include "**/*"

// Ruff N818 (pep8-naming): a class whose name does not end in `Error` though one of its bases is spelled
// `Exception` or `…Error`. Ruff reads the bases as written: a bare name only, not resolved, not `mod.Error`.
//   class C(Exception): ...          ← N818
//   class D(BaseException): ...      not reported: the base is neither
#include "python/naming.rr"

.violation N818(at: node, x: symbol) code "N818"
    "Rename the exception class `{x}` to end in `Error`, e.g. `{x}Error` or swapping an `Exception` suffix for `Error`, and update references; keep it if it signals control flow, not an error."
    suppress ruff "N818"
N818(nm, x) :- kind(c, "class_definition"), field(c, "name", nm), text(nm, x), !suffix("Error", x),
    error_base(c), !naming_ignored(x).
.decl error_base(c: node)  // a positional base that is the name `Exception` or `…Error`
error_base(c) :- field(c, "superclasses", al), child(al, b, _), kind(b, "identifier"), text(b, t),
    (t = "Exception" ; suffix("Error", t)).
